IMPORT prelude

-- Central Provident Fund (Exemption) Order 2018 (S 61/2018), made by the Minister for Manpower under s 69 of the Central
-- Provident Fund Act 1953 -- employers exempted from paying contributions for certain employees.
--
-- EDITION: THE VERSION AS MADE, in force from 1 January to 1 February 2018 (the PDF's own footer), deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/CPFA1953-S61-2018.txt. Later amendments, if any, are not reflected; the current version should
-- be checked (see NOTES.md).
--
-- WHY. Added on 11 October 2026 for REQ-0003 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl (cradle-to-grave-simone, event e032: a
-- full-time university student on a paid internship in May 2025).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: para 2(1)(b) and 2(2) (contributions to the community funds under s 76(3)) except as noted; which institutions
-- fall within each paragraph and whether training is "approved by the institution" are inputs.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Central Provident Fund (Exemption) Order 2018`

§§ `The Schedule, paragraphs 5 to 8 -- students`

-- Para 5: "a matriculated or registered student of any of the following institutions and employed for training approved by the
-- institution concerned: (a) any university whose function of providing university education is determined by any written
-- law; (b) the Institute of Technical Education ...; (c) a polytechnic established by any written law; (d) a school specified in
-- Part II or III of the Schedule to the [Edusave Pupils Fund] Regulations; (e) Mountbatten Vocational School."
-- Para 6: a student of a private education institution, enrolled in a full-time programme subsidised by the Ministry of
-- Education and listed on its website, employed for training approved by the institution.
-- Para 7: a student of an overseas tertiary institution required by it to train in Singapore for not more than 6 months, who
-- gives the employer the institution's written confirmation.
-- Para 8: a registered student of a listed school (other than one who has completed the GCE 'A' Level Examination or its
-- equivalent) employed during a school holiday period.
DECLARE Institution IS ONE OF
    `a university whose function is determined by written law`
    `the Institute of Technical Education`
    `a polytechnic established by written law`
    `a school in Part II or III of the Edusave Schedule`
    `Mountbatten Vocational School`
    `a private education institution`
    `an overseas tertiary education institution`
    `a school listed in paragraph 8`
    `none of these`

DECLARE Student HAS
    `institution` IS A Institution
    `matriculated or registered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed for training approved by the institution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a full-time MOE-subsidised programme listed on the MOE website` IS A BOOLEAN
    `required by the institution to train in Singapore for months` IS A NUMBER
    `gave the employer the institution's written confirmation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has completed the GCE A Level or equivalent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed during a school holiday period` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN i IS A Institution
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a paragraph 5 institution` i IF
       i EQUALS `a university whose function is determined by written law`
    OR i EQUALS `the Institute of Technical Education`
    OR i EQUALS `a polytechnic established by written law`
    OR i EQUALS `a school in Part II or III of the Edusave Schedule`
    OR i EQUALS `Mountbatten Vocational School`

GIVEN s IS A Student
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a specified student employee` s IF
        s's `matriculated or registered`
    AND (    (`is a paragraph 5 institution` (s's `institution`) AND s's `employed for training approved by the institution`)
          OR (    s's `institution` EQUALS `a private education institution`
              AND s's `in a full-time MOE-subsidised programme listed on the MOE website`
              AND s's `employed for training approved by the institution`)
          OR (    s's `institution` EQUALS `an overseas tertiary education institution`
              AND s's `required by the institution to train in Singapore for months` GREATER THAN 0
              AND s's `required by the institution to train in Singapore for months` AT MOST 6
              AND s's `gave the employer the institution's written confirmation`)
          OR (    s's `institution` EQUALS `a school listed in paragraph 8`
              AND NOT s's `has completed the GCE A Level or equivalent`
              AND s's `employed during a school holiday period`))

§§ `The Schedule, paragraphs 1 to 4 and 9 -- other specified employees`

DECLARE `Other specified employee` IS ONE OF
    `a domestic employee working at most 14 hours a week`
    `an employee of the United Nations or its agencies in Singapore`
    `a citizen seaman on Swedish, Norwegian or East Asiatic Co terms`
    `a Seventh-Day Adventist employee engaged abroad and not domiciled here`
    `a trainee at the Singapore Hotel Association Training and Educational Centre`
    `none of the others`

§§ `Paragraphs 2 and 3 -- the exemptions`

-- Para 2(1): an employer "whose employee is specified in the Schedule ... is exempt from paying ... (a) any contribution to the
-- Fund under section 7 of the Act". (2): for a para 5(a) university student the same contributions are exempt (the Order
-- separates them only for the community-fund contributions).
-- Para 3: an employer "is exempt from paying any contribution to the Fund under section 7 of the Act in respect of wages payable
-- to an employee who is not a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore".
GIVEN `citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN, student IS A Student, other IS A `Other specified employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer is exempt from section 7 contributions` `citizen or permanent resident` student other IF
       NOT `citizen or permanent resident`
    OR `is a specified student employee` student
    OR NOT (other EQUALS `none of the others`)

GIVEN `citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN, student IS A Student, other IS A `Other specified employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `CPF contributions are payable on the wages` `citizen or permanent resident` student other IF
    NOT `the employer is exempt from section 7 contributions` `citizen or permanent resident` student other
